<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siddis</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Siddhi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Siddis are a community of African descent in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-asia">South Asia</a>. On the western coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, Siddi rulers of Janjira maintained a naval power. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha Empire</a> note that Maratha fleets challenged Siddi and Portuguese maritime forces along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konkan-coast">Konkan coast</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/siddis.jpg" alt="Siddis" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nagarjun Kandukuru from Bangalore, India · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Siddi_community_(16527139018).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
